<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Alange</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1230</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reconquista">Reconquista</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Alange was fought in 1230 near Alange, in modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/extremadura">Extremadura</a>, between the army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-ix-of-leon">Alfonso IX of León</a> and the forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-hud">Ibn Hud</a>, ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murcia">Murcia</a> and much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>. Alfonso's victory opened the way to the Leonese capture of Mérida and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/badajoz">Badajoz</a> that year, weakening Ibn Hud and carrying the Christian advance into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guadiana">Guadiana</a> valley.</p></div>
